on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-5x-2y+2z=5 \\\\ 4x+3y-3z=1 \\\\ -2x+y+2z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-316998/field-1" "q-316998/field-2" "q-316998/field-3" "q-316998/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7958ef60-8041-535b-bff8-b35e84c54412"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316998"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4518"] :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/ed434344208758284aa0f144676f7dd6498a63faeb0248d18e87c4be6c3d87f2.png)\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+0z=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/b9364923447e278db5ec47bef74e1a05310645b30df22d4ea5efcc0de46c6ed2.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/16cb1608f70821d138f0c6984038bb42d86d9fbf76d560d94d2e25bd6fdb05e0.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/0abbbaf34955fa40d6cdbfa9e16cb1567ee16271d65b4565206a0f2204eedf6d.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/4b915439c3e9922d692aab4205a728160e0a1286f82fa5ebc736460901581147.png)\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4519"] :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ z-x+2=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/c9b7abb2641034c1769c6fe6b13b96edd7ccc282b61424b2031a3d37faa456e4.png)\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/6f1bf319faf8be4a9a79c0a6f9301e6eac48a5b04f66949b679e8445b07e9d9c.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/fc1ac06787ed64ebefbb1a7a82f9bf785525777f61831bbbc39bd25c7e629d5a.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/d0249dcecf6b75cd6ff7c4623beac6fd6cfae64a58d043bb6759440167f40ea1.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/64d1f57717dda57c8a7fbc403728ee9699a22ce995f68a50a0b80f25543fdab6.png)\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
